From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] madsync: make in-process sync opt-in

With in-process NT sync on, a thread blocked in madsync never makes the
server wait that would run a system APC. iOS delivers no SIGUSR1, so the
async completion that copies a named-pipe read's data never runs and the
read returns 0 bytes (ladder rung 4, proc.named_pipe_*). madsync is now
off unless madeira.cfg says inproc-sync = 1.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-bootstrap.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/madsync/madsync.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/madsync/madsync.c b/build/madsync/madsync.c
index 39098d5..79ca132 100644
--- a/build/madsync/madsync.c
+++ b/build/madsync/madsync.c
@@ -125,9 +125,14 @@ int madsync_enabled(void)
     static int state = -1;
     if (state < 0)
     {
-        int on = madeira_cfg_bool( "inproc-sync", 1 );   /* ml1095: madeira.cfg inproc-sync = 0 disables */
+        /* Playport: off unless madeira.cfg says inproc-sync = 1. The server
+         * wakes an in-process wait only for user APCs (alert_sync); a system
+         * APC such as an async I/O completion needs SIGUSR1, which iOS never
+         * delivers, so a thread blocked here never copies a pipe read's data
+         * (ladder rung 4, proc.named_pipe_*: 0 bytes). */
+        int on = madeira_cfg_bool( "inproc-sync", 0 );
         state = on;
-        dprintf( 2, "[madsync] ml1058 in-process synchronisation %s (madeira.cfg inproc-sync = 0 disables)\n",
+        dprintf( 2, "[madsync] ml1058 in-process synchronisation %s (madeira.cfg inproc-sync = 1 enables)\n",
                  on ? "ENABLED" : "disabled" );
     }
     return state;
